       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum labeled daily dose. It adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and it substantially raises the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate, so I'm not comfortable placing it as written.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 400 to 600 mg PO four times daily, with GI protection if indicated.\n- **Enter it with a note,** if the order came from a protocol or study I don't know about. Tell me the indication and I'll document it so pharmacy can review.\n- **Suggest alternatives.** If pain control is the goal, I can enter scheduled acetaminophen alongside the ibuprofen, or another agent.\n\nIf you decide to go ahead with the original dose, you'll need to enter it yourself through the standard override and pharmacy verification process. Which of these would you like?"
